# The open channel (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "The open channel"): a radio with "Call on the open channel".
# No body, no faction. A public node goes out on air to everyone within the channel's reach, as
# one line, with no name: nobody's name goes on air (the lint refuses {player}, {name} and the like
# here). Nobody is threatened on air. Every line is a voice on the channel, spoken: no narration.

conv radio.open.call_in
for radio:open
topic "Anyone on this? I've got road news."
prio world
voice plain

node start
  say Go ahead, caller, and keep it short. Batteries are the one thing nobody in the Zone is making any more. What have you seen, and where?
  > @thick {here}'s thick with them. Go round. -> thick   if town:infection>=60
  > @quiet {here} is quiet. For now. -> quiet   if town:infection<60
  > @nothing Nothing. Just checking anyone's there. -> anyone

node thick public
  say Copy that. {here} is thick with them, go round it. Everyone listening, you heard the caller. Thanks, whoever you are.
  do rumour:"Someone on the open channel says {here} is thick with them. Go round."@4
  > @out Out. -> hub

node quiet public
  say Copy. {here} is quiet, for now. Nobody on this channel believes in for now any more, but thank you all the same.
  do rumour:"Someone on the open channel says {here} is quiet, for now."@4
  > @out2 Thanks. Out. -> hub

node anyone
  say Someone's always here, caller. Most nights that's all this channel's for: so nobody listening in a dark house thinks they're the last one left.
  > @out3 Good to hear. Out. -> hub

conv radio.open.listen
for radio:open
topic "Is anyone out there?"
prio flavour
voice plain

node start
  say? night :: Nine. Ten. That's the night watch counted at our end, ten of us on the wall. Is anyone counting at yours? Anyone? All right. One. Two.
  say? mood:hope :: Is it true, then, about the cure? My neighbour says the lab's nearly there. I say they've said that before. We've argued about it all week, and we're both happier for it.
  say? mood:bleak :: This is for anyone near the square. Has anybody seen a brown dog with one white ear? He answers to Bruno. My daughter keeps asking. If you see him, that's all. Thank you.
  say If you can hear this, the houses are open. Bring water if you can. Bring yourself either way. The Haven keeps a bed and a bowl for anyone who'll work.
  > @answer Heard you. Still here. -> answered
  > @off Nothing for me tonight. Out. -> hub

node answered public
  say Good. Good. Keep being still here, whoever you are. That's all anyone on this channel is asking for.
  > @out Out. -> hub

conv radio.open.toll
for radio:open
topic "Red Hand, what's the toll today?"
prio flavour
voice redhand

node start
  say Who's asking? Never mind. Toll for you is {toll} Favor at every lorry, same as yesterday. Prices only go one way on this channel, sweetheart, and it isn't down.
  > @haggle That's too much. Half, and I'll pay now. -> haggle
  > @fine Fine. Out. -> hub

node haggle
  say Half! Lads, it's asked for half. Love the nerve. Still {toll}. Come and argue at the barrier if you like. We've got chairs, a kettle and six blokes who don't haggle.
  > @out Out. -> hub

# A distress call (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "The radio"): someone near a Haven house asking for help, an hour
# in two. Answering sends them to that house's gate, where errands deal its gate card (Who's at the
# Gate) under errands' own rules and pay. Once a real hour per player; nothing personal on air.
conv radio.open.distress
for radio:open
when distress
topic "I'm on. Who's calling for help?"
prio ask
voice plain

node start
  say Anyone on this. Two of us, on foot near {distress}. The car's done, the light's going, and we've been hearing them in the trees for an hour.
  say We don't need much. Just which way to somewhere with a door that bolts and people behind it.
  > @house Make for {distress}. Knock twice. -> sent   do call:distress
  > @hurt Is anyone hurt? Anyone bitten? -> hurt   if bg:doctor,nurse
  > @sorry I can't get to you. Sorry. -> sorry

node hurt
  say Her ankle. She went over on it in a ditch. Not a bite, she says, and I looked. I believe her, near enough. She can walk if I hold her up.
  > @house2 Make for {distress}. Mind the ankle. -> sent   do call:distress
  > @sorry2 I'm sorry. I can't get to you. -> sorry

node sent public
  say Copy. The Haven house at {distress}, knock twice, and say the radio sent us. Thank you. Thank you, whoever you are.
  > @out Out. -> hub

node sorry
  say Right. We'll walk, then, and keep off the road. Thanks for answering. Most nights nobody does.
  > @out2 Out. -> hub
